{
  "$comment": "#EXP-1832 SIDEBAR FOLDERS + DRAG REORDER, x4 (web `lib/sidebar-layout.ts` + the sidebar groups, desktop `domain::sidebar_folders`, iOS ExpCore `SidebarFolders.swift`, Android `domain/SidebarFolders.kt`; the pure reference is `src/sidebar-folders.ts`; every mirror replays every list here and compares the WHOLE expected value). SCOPE: the sidebar's Boards, Agents and Apps groups (one SECTION each: board, agent, app); the Chats list is untouched. Each MEMBER arranges their own sidebar; the layout syncs to their devices. Drag happens on the desktop IDE and wide web only; phones (the board pickers, the Apps list) show the folders read-only. A row moves only within its own section. STORAGE: the synced per-user `sidebar_layout` table (shape = static `user_id = me`, like pins): one row per node, `kind` folder | item, an item's `target_id` (the board / agent / app), its `parent_id` (the folder; null = top level), a folder's `name`, a fractional `sort_order`. TREE (`tree`, sidebarTree(items, entries)): `items` = the section's visible targets in DEFAULT order (boards and agents by sortOrder, apps by name). Placed nodes (folders, items with an entry) come first by sortOrder, ties by entry id; every item with NO entry follows in default order (so nothing jumps on deploy, and a new board lands at the end). An entry whose target is not visible is skipped; an item whose parent names no folder sits at the top level; TWO LAYERS MAX: a folder holds items only and its own parent is ignored; a folder with no visible item is not shown; a folder with no name shows `New folder`. MOVE (`move`, sidebarMove): the genUI List's `move` event {id, before | after | into} (exactly one), ids = node ids (an item = its target id, a folder = its entry id). before/after = beside the target in the target's container (beside a folder's item = into that folder); into a FOLDER = appended to it; into a top-level ITEM = a NEW folder (`newFolderId`, minted by the client, named `New folder`) at the item's place holding the item, then the dragged row; the client then edits the name in place (Enter saves, Esc keeps the default). Refused (null, nothing written): an unknown id, onto itself, not exactly one position, a folder into anything, a folder beside a folder's item, into an item that already sits in a folder. A folder the move EMPTIES is deleted (`deletes`). The result is the WRITES: every node's sort_order = its 1-based index in its container, and only rows that differ from their entry (or have none: `id` null = a new item entry, upserted by (user, section, target)), in tree order. UNGROUP (`ungroup`, a folder's right-click menu): its items take its place at the top level in order and the folder is deleted. RENAME (`folderNames`): trimmed, at most 80 characters, empty = `New folder`. ROWS (`rows`, sidebarRows): what a client's List gets, one row per visible node: depth 0 | 1, a folder row `group: true` with its item count, a CLOSED folder's items left out. The expanded flag is LOCAL per device (localStorage, the IDE settings file, UserDefaults, DataStore) under `openKeys` (team + folder); no stored flag = open. A folder row is never navigable: a press folds it.",
  "maxDepth": 2,
  "defaultFolderName": "New folder",
  "tree": [
    {"name": "no entries keep the default order", "items": ["exponential", "feedback", "errors", "performance", "next"], "entries": [], "expected": [{"kind": "item", "id": "exponential"}, {"kind": "item", "id": "feedback"}, {"kind": "item", "id": "errors"}, {"kind": "item", "id": "performance"}, {"kind": "item", "id": "next"}]},
    {"name": "placed items by sortOrder, unplaced after them in default order", "items": ["exponential", "feedback", "errors", "performance", "next"], "entries": [{"id": "e-next", "kind": "item", "targetId": "next", "parentId": null, "name": null, "sortOrder": 1}, {"id": "e-err", "kind": "item", "targetId": "errors", "parentId": null, "name": null, "sortOrder": 2}], "expected": [{"kind": "item", "id": "next"}, {"kind": "item", "id": "errors"}, {"kind": "item", "id": "exponential"}, {"kind": "item", "id": "feedback"}, {"kind": "item", "id": "performance"}]},
    {"name": "a folder holds its items in their own order", "items": ["exponential", "feedback", "errors", "performance", "next"], "entries": [{"id": "e-exp", "kind": "item", "targetId": "exponential", "parentId": null, "name": null, "sortOrder": 1}, {"id": "e-feed", "kind": "item", "targetId": "feedback", "parentId": null, "name": null, "sortOrder": 2}, {"id": "f-mon", "kind": "folder", "targetId": null, "parentId": null, "name": "Monitoring", "sortOrder": 3}, {"id": "e-err", "kind": "item", "targetId": "errors", "parentId": "f-mon", "name": null, "sortOrder": 1}, {"id": "e-perf", "kind": "item", "targetId": "performance", "parentId": "f-mon", "name": null, "sortOrder": 2}, {"id": "e-next", "kind": "item", "targetId": "next", "parentId": null, "name": null, "sortOrder": 4}], "expected": [{"kind": "item", "id": "exponential"}, {"kind": "item", "id": "feedback"}, {"kind": "folder", "id": "f-mon", "name": "Monitoring", "children": ["errors", "performance"]}, {"kind": "item", "id": "next"}]},
    {"name": "an entry whose target is gone is skipped; a folder with no visible item is hidden", "items": ["exponential", "feedback", "next"], "entries": [{"id": "e-exp", "kind": "item", "targetId": "exponential", "parentId": null, "name": null, "sortOrder": 1}, {"id": "e-feed", "kind": "item", "targetId": "feedback", "parentId": null, "name": null, "sortOrder": 2}, {"id": "f-mon", "kind": "folder", "targetId": null, "parentId": null, "name": "Monitoring", "sortOrder": 3}, {"id": "e-err", "kind": "item", "targetId": "errors", "parentId": "f-mon", "name": null, "sortOrder": 1}, {"id": "e-perf", "kind": "item", "targetId": "performance", "parentId": "f-mon", "name": null, "sortOrder": 2}, {"id": "e-next", "kind": "item", "targetId": "next", "parentId": null, "name": null, "sortOrder": 4}, {"id": "f-old", "kind": "folder", "targetId": null, "parentId": null, "name": "Old", "sortOrder": 5}, {"id": "e-gone", "kind": "item", "targetId": "gone", "parentId": "f-old", "name": null, "sortOrder": 1}], "expected": [{"kind": "item", "id": "exponential"}, {"kind": "item", "id": "feedback"}, {"kind": "item", "id": "next"}]},
    {"name": "an item whose folder is gone sits at the top level", "items": ["exponential", "feedback"], "entries": [{"id": "e-exp", "kind": "item", "targetId": "exponential", "parentId": "f-missing", "name": null, "sortOrder": 2}, {"id": "e-feed", "kind": "item", "targetId": "feedback", "parentId": null, "name": null, "sortOrder": 1}], "expected": [{"kind": "item", "id": "feedback"}, {"kind": "item", "id": "exponential"}]},
    {"name": "a folder never nests: its parentId is ignored", "items": ["exponential", "feedback", "next"], "entries": [{"id": "f-a", "kind": "folder", "targetId": null, "parentId": null, "name": "A", "sortOrder": 1}, {"id": "f-b", "kind": "folder", "targetId": null, "parentId": "f-a", "name": "B", "sortOrder": 2}, {"id": "e-exp", "kind": "item", "targetId": "exponential", "parentId": "f-a", "name": null, "sortOrder": 1}, {"id": "e-feed", "kind": "item", "targetId": "feedback", "parentId": "f-b", "name": null, "sortOrder": 1}], "expected": [{"kind": "folder", "id": "f-a", "name": "A", "children": ["exponential"]}, {"kind": "folder", "id": "f-b", "name": "B", "children": ["feedback"]}, {"kind": "item", "id": "next"}]},
    {"name": "equal sortOrder ties by entry id", "items": ["exponential", "feedback"], "entries": [{"id": "e-b", "kind": "item", "targetId": "exponential", "parentId": null, "name": null, "sortOrder": 1}, {"id": "e-a", "kind": "item", "targetId": "feedback", "parentId": null, "name": null, "sortOrder": 1}], "expected": [{"kind": "item", "id": "feedback"}, {"kind": "item", "id": "exponential"}]},
    {"name": "a folder with no name shows the default", "items": ["exponential"], "entries": [{"id": "f-x", "kind": "folder", "targetId": null, "parentId": null, "name": null, "sortOrder": 1}, {"id": "e-exp", "kind": "item", "targetId": "exponential", "parentId": "f-x", "name": null, "sortOrder": 1}], "expected": [{"kind": "folder", "id": "f-x", "name": "New folder", "children": ["exponential"]}]}
